  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the National HIV and Tuberculosis Programmes in scaling up treatment and care services nationwide - Djibouti (01-Jul-2018-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Djibouti, TB/HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Djibouti)This program has the following goals: To reduce the prevalence of tuberculosis by 25% by 2025.  To halve new HIV infections by 2022.  To improve the life expectancy and quality of life for people infected and affected by HIV and comorbidity agents. The objectives of this program are: To improve screening for new cases of tuberculosis with a view to reporting 3200 new cases by 2020.  To improve treatment success to achieve a rate in excess of 85% from 2016 and to maintain it at that level until 2020.  To ensure that the prevalence of primary resistance amongst new cases does not exceed 1.8% between now and 2020.  To reduce the death rate among cases of co-infection from 17% to 15% by 2020.  For the incidence of HIV to halve by 2022.  For the HIV mortality rate to be reduced by 70% by 2022</narrative>
  </description>
